{"kind":"request","text":"XD-1 step 1b: the Native timeout guard names the test that owns the timer (ruling 925778a5).\n\nThe guard reports the test whose context owns the aborted controller, not the test that `expect.getState()` names when the timer fires. A controller that no context registered reports `(no owner)`. The Node control pins it: a timer that test A starts and that fires during test B names A. The XD-1 note's \"Read the line\" section says how to read a line.\n\nDone when the head passes one gate, the gate's crossing lines name their owners, and the checker approves. Step 2 (repair each named case) and step 3 (a crossing fails the gate) are not part of this request.","body":{"conditions":"one gate passes; crossing lines name the owning test; Node control pins A-then-B; checker approval","target_head":"d6c863bb9dcd961c13f718ef6cd2851bdd18a13e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}